Generic single-database configuration.

Production migrations must follow expand-and-contract and remain compatible with the currently running application and the immediately previous immutable image.

Add new tables and nullable columns first, deploy code that can use both schema versions, backfill separately, and remove old columns or constraints only in a later release after all application instances have stopped using them.

Do not rely on database downgrade during normal rollback.
If a schema change is not backward-compatible, prefer a forward-fix migration
and a corrected application image.

CI runs `alembic upgrade head` and `alembic check` against PostgreSQL.
It also examines newly changed migration upgrades for dropped tables or columns, unsafe non-null additions, in-place type changes, and destructive raw SQL.
An exceptional operation requires an adjacent `# migration-safety: allow <reason>` marker and explicit review.
